# The readFromFile simulation doesn't generate EOS tokens! That's because
# our new readWord when it encounters '\n' generates EOS, but the '\n' isn't 
# being encountered here because after 'acting' the stream has '\n' followed by
# 'terrible', and when we read 'acting' we consume the space before '\n'...
# Actually wait: the stream has "great acting\n". 
# After reading "great" (stops at ' '), the stream has " acting\n"
# After reading "acting" (skip ' ', read 'a','c','t','i','n','g', then peek '\n' -> break)
# Wait: after reading the word chars, we do "if (std::isspace(c)) break"
# When reading "acting", we read: 'a','c','t','i','n','g' and then '\n' is encountered
# '\n' is whitespace so we break AFTER consuming '\n'!
# 
# Hmm, actually: "while ((c = in.get()) != EOF) { if (std::isspace(c)) break; word += c; }"
# After reading 'g', we call in.get() which gives '\n', which isspace -> break
# '\n' is consumed! So the next readWord won't see it.
# 
# That's why EOS isn't being generated - the '\n' after each line is consumed by
# the word-reading loop!
#
# Fix: Don't consume '\n' in the word-reading loop, use peek instead
# OR: When we consume '\n' in the word-reading loop, add EOS ourselves

